n and drop  the camera run away is you're there to  document what happened  foreign  [Applause]  what happened  it collapsed  the top floors collapsed down  the sword brought blow and then ran like  hell thank God  I'm 69 but I can still run  Trap Back Then  when the second tower fell  I thought that La ganga had probably  bought it that uh that was it  and I was thinking about having to speak  with his wife about that  but I remained hopeful and I moved  forward  to find him  and at some point  Mark came walking out covered Head To  Toe with the dust of the Tower and a  gash on his forehead but he came out and  we washed them off and kept going  what'd you see everything that's a chaos  it's just chaos out here it really is so  the Twin Towers full it was beeping all  around us the sounds we heard all around  us of beeping  were alarms from the clothing or on the  person's the fire fighters  the beeping is fire I didn't know this  at the time but it's a sound you can  never forget it's a firefighter down  alarm and it means there are  firefighters trapped  [Music]  nice  [Music]  there are people who did amazing things  that day I literally just videotaped  what they were doing  do you have survivor's count  no yes I I don't know how to answer that  yeah I mean I don't think anyone that  was there that day doesn't feel guilty  that they were able to go home people  went towards the building to save people  I just videotaped so I feel pretty  guilty about that I really don't think  he can indict himself for doing his job  that day  I think he did a service to us all by  continuing to go forward  I hope we're all a little bit better  because we're able to see  [Music]  what people do in that kind of situation  and all I saw was people helping each  other I never saw anything else there  was a time immediately after the towers  fell when there was a cohesiveness in  the city you could feel it  still the greatest City I mean I know  sounds glib to say that but I mean i